# ACME Team Management — Frontend Structure

This document defines the page inventory, navigation, RBAC rules, and key UI patterns for the React frontend.

---

## 1. Role Definitions

The application recognizes five effective user types, derived from the `roles[]` array and `staffType` field on the `individuals` collection.

| User type | Determined by | Description |
|-----------|--------------|-------------|
| **System admin** | `roles` includes `system_admin` | Full access to everything. Sees the admin sidebar. Can CRUD all entities. |
| **Team lead** | `roles` includes `team_lead` | Manages their own team: members, achievements, history. Read-only view of other teams. |
| **Editor (direct)** | `roles` includes `editor` + `staffType: "direct"` | Can view own team and edit their own profile. Read-only for team data. |
| **Viewer (direct)** | `roles` includes `viewer` + `staffType: "direct"` | Same screens as editor but everything is read-only, including own profile. |
| **Non-direct** | `staffType: "non-direct"` (any role) | Restricted read-only placeholder. Sees own team and achievements. Cannot edit profile. |

**Role resolution priority:** If a user has multiple roles (e.g., `["team_lead", "editor"]`), the highest-privilege role wins for navigation. The sidebar shows the most permissive set of pages the user can access.

