## 3. Page Specifications

### 3.1 Global Dashboard (`/admin/dashboard`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Bird's-eye view of all teams, surfacing the business metrics from the requirements.

**KPI Cards (top row):**
- Total active teams
- Total active individuals (with direct vs. non-direct split)
- Teams with leader not co-located (count + list on click)
- Teams with non-direct leader (count + list on click)
- Teams with non-direct ratio > 20% (count + list on click)

**Charts / Sections:**
- Teams by region (NAM / LATAM / EU / APAC) — bar or donut chart
- Recent achievements feed (last 30 days, across all teams)
- Teams reporting to each senior leader — grouped list

**Interactions:**
- Click any KPI card → filtered view of the relevant teams
- Click a team name anywhere → navigate to `/admin/teams/:id`

---

### 3.2 All Teams (`/admin/teams`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Searchable, filterable table of all teams.

**Table Columns:**
- Team name
- Home location (with region badge)
- Leader name + co-location indicator
- Active member count (with cap indicator: "4/5")
- Non-direct ratio (with warning badge if > 20%)
- Reports to (current org leader)

**Filters:**
- Region (multi-select: NAM, LATAM, EU, APAC)
- Non-direct ratio threshold (slider or checkbox for "> 20%")
- Leader co-location (co-located / not co-located / all)

**Actions:**
- Create Team button → modal or new page
- Click row → `/admin/teams/:id`
- Soft-delete (with confirmation dialog)

---

### 3.3 Team Detail (`/admin/teams/:id` or `/teams/:id` read-only)

**Purpose:** Complete view of a single team.

**Tabs:**
1. **Overview** — Team name, home location (map pin optional), current reporting line, created date
2. **Members** — Roster table: name, role, staff type snapshot, location, start date, status (active/departed). Admin and team lead see add/remove buttons. Shows "X/5 members" cap indicator.
3. **Achievements** — Monthly grouped list. Admin and team lead see create/edit. Others see read-only.
4. **History** — Timeline view of `teamHistory` events. Admin and team lead only.

**Sidebar card (always visible):**
- Leader name + avatar/initials
- Leader co-location status
- Leader staff type
- Non-direct ratio gauge

---

### 3.4 All Individuals (`/admin/individuals`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Search and manage all people in the system.

**Table Columns:**
- Name
- Email
- Primary location
- Staff type (badge: direct / non-direct)
- Role(s) (badges)
- Team(s) — comma-separated list of active teams

**Search:** Fuzzy search on name and email.

**Filters:**
- Staff type (direct / non-direct)
- Role (multi-select)
- Location (multi-select)

**Actions:**
- Create Individual button
- Click row → `/admin/individuals/:id`
- Soft-delete (with confirmation)

---

### 3.5 Individual Profile (`/admin/individuals/:id` or `/profile`)

**Purpose:** View and edit personal info.

**Sections:**
1. **Header** — Avatar/initials, name, job title, email, location
2. **Details** — Staff type, role(s), created date, last login
3. **Team Memberships** — List of active teams with role on each team. Links to team detail.
4. **Edit Form** (admin or own profile with editor role) — Name, email, job title, location picker, staff type (admin only), roles (admin only)

**Access rules:**
- Admin: can edit everything
- Team lead / editor: can edit own name, email, job title, location
- Viewer: read-only
- Non-direct: read-only

---

### 3.6 All Achievements (`/admin/achievements`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Cross-team achievement feed with full CRUD.

**Layout:** Card-based feed, grouped by month (YYYY-MM).

**Each Card:**
- Achievement title + description
- Team name (linked)
- Impact metric (highlighted)
- Tags (pill badges)
- Contributors (avatar row, linked to profiles)
- Proof link (if present)
- Created by + date

**Filters:**
- Team (multi-select)
- Month (date picker)
- Tag (multi-select, populated from existing tags)

---

### 3.7 My Team Dashboard (`/team/dashboard`) — Team Lead

**Purpose:** Focused view of the lead's own team.

**KPI Cards:**
- Active members (X/5 cap)
- Non-direct ratio (with gauge)
- Achievements this month (count)
- Leader co-location status

**Sections:**
- Quick member roster (with manage link)
- Recent achievements (last 3)
- Current reporting line

---

### 3.8 Manage Members (`/team/members`) — Team Lead

**Purpose:** Add/remove members, assign delegate.

**Table:** Same as team detail members tab but with action buttons.

**Actions:**
- Add Member — search individuals, select, confirm. Shows cap warning if at 4/5.
- Remove Member — sets endDate, writes teamHistory event.
- Assign Delegate — select from current members.
- Cap indicator at top: "4/5 members — 1 slot remaining"

**Validation messages:**
- "This team already has 5 active members" (blocks add)
- "This person is already on this team" (blocks duplicate)
- "A delegate is already assigned" (blocks second delegate)

---

### 3.9 Team Achievements (`/team/achievements`) — Team Lead (edit) / Members (read)

**Purpose:** Manage achievements for the lead's team.

**Layout:** Same card feed as admin achievements but scoped to one team.

**Create Achievement Form (team lead only):**
- Title (required)
- Description (required)
- Achievement month (YYYY-MM picker, defaults to current month)
- Impact metric
- Tags (comma-separated or tag picker)
- Contributors (multi-select from team members + search all individuals for cross-team contributors)
- Proof link

---

### 3.10 Achievements Feed (`/achievements`) — Editor / Viewer / Non-Direct

**Purpose:** Read-only achievements for motivation and visibility.

**Content:**
- **Own team achievements** — all achievements for teams the user belongs to
- **Shared achievements** — achievements from other teams where at least one contributor is also a member of the user's team. This creates a natural cross-team visibility based on overlapping people, not arbitrary broadcast.

**Layout:** Card feed, grouped by month. Team name badge on each card distinguishes own team vs. shared.

**Filter:** Month picker, own team only vs. all visible.

---

### 3.11 My Teammates (`/team/people`) — Editor / Viewer

**Purpose:** See who's on the team.

**Layout:** Card grid (not table — more personal/visual feel).

**Each Card:**
- Initials avatar
- Name
- Job title
- Role on team (Member / Team Leader / Delegate)
- Location + region badge
- Staff type badge

Click → mini profile modal (name, email, location, teams — read-only).

---

### 3.12 Locations (`/admin/locations`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Manage the controlled list of office locations.

**Table Columns:** Name, city, country, region, timezone.

**Actions:** Create, edit, soft-delete. Region is a dropdown (NAM/LATAM/EU/APAC).

---

### 3.13 Reports (`/admin/reports`) — Admin Only

**Purpose:** Answer the business questions from the requirements.

**Pre-built report cards:**

1. **Teams by region** — Count + list per region
2. **Leader co-location** — Which teams have their leader in a different location than the team home
3. **Leader staff type** — Which teams have a non-direct leader
4. **Non-direct ratio** — Teams sorted by ratio, flagging those above 20%
5. **Reporting line summary** — Teams grouped by who they report to
6. **Multi-team members** — Individuals active on more than one team

Each report is a collapsible section or tab. Data is derived from the existing collections (no separate reporting tables).

